all points of \\(S_n\\) and containing precisely the prescribed number \\(k\\) of sunny lines.\n\n10. **Impossibility of other values of \\(k\\).**  \n    The total number of lines is fixed to be \\(n\\); a line is either sunny or non‑sunny, so \\(k\\) must satisfy \\(0\\le k\\le n\\).  \n    The constructions above show that every integer in this interval is attainable.  \n    Hence no other values of \\(k\\) are possible.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{For every }n\\ge3\\text{ and every }k\\in\\{0,1,\\dots ,n\\}\\text{ there exists a suitable family of }n\\text{ lines, and only these }k\\text{ are possible.}}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
